# CODEOWNERS — makes the three freeze signatures enforceable through GitHub itself.
# Replace the placeholders with real GitHub handles/teams, then in repo settings:
#   1. Protect the main branch: require pull-request reviews from Code Owners.
#   2. Protect the tag pattern  prd/**  (Settings -> Rules -> Rulesets -> New tag ruleset;
#      '**' matters, releases tag as prd/<slug>/r<N>, two levels deep) so release tags
#      can't be moved or deleted — that tag is the immutable Handoff Release.
# With this, a freeze PR cannot merge until PM + Tech Lead + QA have all approved
# with their own GitHub identities, commit-bound — no editable names in YAML.

# Everything needs the PM (bundle owner)
*                     @pm-handle

# Behaviour + handoff need the Tech Lead
SPEC.md               @pm-handle @tech-lead-handle
HANDOFF.md             @pm-handle @tech-lead-handle
contracts/             @tech-lead-handle

# Coverage, evidence and reconcile need QA
EVIDENCE/              @pm-handle @qa-handle
TRACKING.md            @pm-handle @qa-handle

# The manifest carries the release block — all three sign
prd.manifest.yaml      @pm-handle @tech-lead-handle @qa-handle
